const methodology=`<h3>Sets</h3><p>Hevy’s exercise-level primary and secondary muscle mappings. Normal and failure sets count; warm-ups and empty sets do not. Drop segments remain separate. Secondary work is not added to direct sets.</p><h3>Regions</h3><p>Regional counts describe exercise emphasis, not isolated muscle activation or measured growth. Incline chest work is tagged upper, dips/decline lower, and standard horizontal bench presses, Hevy’s chest-press / iso-lateral chest-press machines and machine chest flies mid. This uses the standard horizontal setup for those named templates; a different seat or machine angle can change the emphasis. Unrecognized custom chest movements remain general. Shoulder presses, lateral raises and rear-delt movements are similarly grouped by emphasis.</p><p>Other anatomical subdivisions can be explored visually, but their set counts cannot be separated from the log. The panel explicitly shows group totals for those regions. Left and right are highlighted together.</p><p><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33049982/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Bench-angle study</a> · <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34644424/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Regional pectoralis study</a></p><h3>Data</h3><p>Workouts are cached only in this browser. With Hevy sign-in, a Vercel function processes your password once and reads your workouts; passwords and workouts are not saved on the server. Access and refresh tokens are encrypted in an HttpOnly browser cookie, valid for up to 30 days. With an API key, the key stays in this browser and sync connects directly to Hevy. Disconnect clears the session cookie and this device’s cached data. This web-login integration is unofficial and may need updating if Hevy changes its website. Periods end on the latest loaded workout; dates use your device timezone. CSV dates without a timezone use your device timezone. The figure is an anatomical reference, not a body scan.</p><h3>Anatomy</h3><p><a href="https://github.com/Charleeh/ecorche" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Écorché</a> by Charleeh, CC BY-SA 4.0. Based on BodyParts3D © The Database Center for Life Science, CC BY 4.0, and Z-Anatomy by Gauthier Kervyn, CC BY-SA 4.0. Geometry unchanged; materials and training associations customized.</p><p><a href="./assets/ATTRIBUTION.md" target="_blank">Credits</a> · <a href="./assets/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt" target="_blank">Model license</a> · <a href="./vendor/THREE-LICENSE.txt" target="_blank">Three.js license</a></p>`;
$('#region-info').onclick=()=>showDialog('<h2>Exercise emphasis</h2>'+methodology);
